{"parentUuid":"1844b192-b5c3-4256-a817-2ae3f4609cfa","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/admin/project/shopping-k8s-manifest/.claude/worktrees/legacy-sync","sessionId":"4ef2b2fb-d3c8-4ec8-bd70-451919a8b76c","version":"2.1.50","gitBranch":"worktree-legacy-sync","agentId":"a11160ef0215536a5","slug":"jazzy-jumping-fairy","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011R1UE289GzZUSN9HyqnkSA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've explored the `apps/next-search/shared-resources/` directory thoroughly. Here's a comprehensive summary of what I found:\n\n## Directory Structure\n\n```\napps/next-search/shared-resources/\n├── Chart.yaml\n├── templates/\n│   └── configmap.yaml\n└── values/\n    ├── values-dev.yaml\n    └── values-prod.yaml\n```\n\n## 1. Chart.yaml\n\n**Location:** `/Users/admin/project/shopping-k8s-manifest/.claude/worktrees/legacy-sync/apps/next-search/shared-resources/Chart.yaml`\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: v2\nname: shared-resources\ndescription: Common ConfigMap and resources for next-search services\ntype: application\nversion: 0.1.0\n```\n\nThis is a Helm chart that provides shared configuration resources for the next-search services.\n\n## 2. Template Files\n\n**Location:** `/Users/admin/project/shopping-k8s-manifest/.claude/worktrees/legacy-sync/apps/next-search/shared-resources/templates/configmap.yaml`\n\nThe template defines a single **ConfigMap** with the following structure:\n\n- **ConfigMap Name:** Defaults to `cmn-search-config` (can be overridden via `configMapName` value)\n- **Namespace:** Uses the Helm release namespace\n\n### ConfigMap Data Structure\n\nThe ConfigMap contains environment variables organized by infrastructure component:\n\n**Elasticsearch Configuration:**\n- `ELASTICSEARCH_URLS`\n- `ELASTICSEARCH_CONNECTION_TIMEOUT`\n- `ELASTICSEARCH_SOCKET_TIMEOUT`\n\n**Valkey Front Cluster:** (Note: This section is NOT in values-dev or values-prod, so it won't be rendered)\n- `VALKEY_FRONT_HOST`\n- `VALKEY_FRONT_PORT`\n- `VALKEY_FRONT_DATABASE`\n- `VALKEY_FRONT_MAX_CONNECTION`\n- `VALKEY_FRONT_CLUSTER_MODE`\n\n**Valkey Backend Cluster:**\n- `VALKEY_BACKEND_HOST`\n- `VALKEY_BACKEND_PORT`\n- `VALKEY_BACKEND_DATABASE`\n- `VALKEY_BACKEND_MAX_CONNECTION`\n- `VALKEY_BACKEND_CLUSTER_MODE`\n\n**MongoDB Configuration:** (Not in current values files)\n- `MONGODB_BACKEND_URL`\n- `MONGODB_BACKEND_DB`\n\n**Keyword Analysis Configuration:**\n- `KEYWORD_ANALYSIS_URL`\n- `KEYWORD_ANALYSIS_CONNECTION_TIMEOUT`\n- `KEYWORD_ANALYSIS_SOCKET_TIMEOUT`\n\n## 3. Values Files\n\n### values-dev.yaml\n\n**Location:** `/Users/admin/project/shopping-k8s-manifest/.claude/worktrees/legacy-sync/apps/next-search/shared-resources/values/values-dev.yaml`\n\n```yaml\nconfigMapName: dev-cmn-search-config\n\nelasticsearch:\n  urls: \"http://dev-cmn-es-http:9200\"\n  connectionTimeout: \"5000\"\n  socketTimeout: \"5000\"\n\nvalkey:\n  backend:\n    host: \"dev-cmn-infra-valkey-cluster-headless.cmn-infra.svc.cluster.local\"\n    port: \"6379\"\n    database: \"0\"\n    maxConnection: \"10\"\n    clusterMode: \"true\"\n\nkeywordAnalysis:\n  url: \"http://dev-cmn-es-data:9200\"\n  connectionTimeout: \"5000\"\n  socketTimeout: \"5000\"\n```\n\n### values-prod.yaml\n\n**Location:** `/Users/admin/project/shopping-k8s-manifest/.claude/worktrees/legacy-sync/apps/next-search/shared-resources/values/values-prod.yaml`\n\n```yaml\nelasticsearch:\n  urls: \"http://cmn-elasticsearch.danuricorp.com:80\"\n  connectionTimeout: \"5000\"\n  socketTimeout: \"5000\"\n\nvalkey:\n  backend:\n    host: \"cmn-valkey.danuricorp.com\"\n    port: \"6379\"\n    database: \"0\"\n    maxConnection: \"10\"\n    clusterMode: \"true\"\n\nkeywordAnalysis:\n  url: \"http://cmn-keyword-analysis-api.danuricorp.com:80\"\n  connectionTimeout: \"5000\"\n  socketTimeout: \"5000\"\n```\n\n## Key Observations\n\n1. **Minimal Templating:** The chart only contains a single ConfigMap template. The `valkey.front` and `mongodb` sections are defined in the template but have no corresponding values, so they won't be rendered.\n\n2. **Environment-Specific Configuration:** Dev uses Kubernetes internal DNS names (e.g., `dev-cmn-es-http:9200`), while prod uses external domain names (e.g., `cmn-elasticsearch.danuricorp.com:80`).\n\n3. **ConfigMap Naming:** Dev explicitly names it `dev-cmn-search-config`, while prod omits the `configMapName`, causing it to default to `cmn-search-config`.\n\n4. **Timeouts:** Both environments use identical timeout settings (5000ms for both connection and socket timeouts).\n\n5. **Valkey Backend:** Only the backend cluster configuration is actively used; the front cluster section exists in the template but has no values defined."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1832,"cache_read_input_tokens":30265,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1832},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CYQR3nsne684yT9CBu2pR","type":"assistant","uuid":"f442aa53-2cdc-4c92-82c5-1eb15948d714","timestamp":"2026-02-23T05:03:22.051Z"}
